SUMMARY:Breaking Rules Breaks Barriers
DESCRIPTION:Whose permission are you waiting for?  \nThis conversation reflects on entrepreneurship\, reinvention\, and the courage to challenge convention. Spanning four decades\, three very different journeys\, and two continents\, the session explores how one woman built a technology company in the United States while navigating ambition\, family\, and personal change. \nThe session is also\, in part\, a homecoming: a story that began with leaving India more than fifty years ago\, now returning to be told in Bangalore\, the heart of the country’s technology world. It makes the case for being a little edgy\, for refusing to wait for anyone’s permission to break from convention. \nPresented by: \n \nVenue: Library\n\n\nEntrepreneurship\, Reinvention and Finding Your Own Path\nRSVP here (https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdk7tNiLKQu06ROlcv89XfXPqJ1xab4bqUA4_lfVL3dw_fdyw/viewform?usp=pp_url)\n*Speakers*: Vinita Gupta\, Ranjeet Pratap Singh\, Sandeep Singhal\, Priya Chetty-Rajagopal\n*Event Categories*: Books\, Business\, Gender
URL:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/event/breaking-rules-breaks-barriers/
LOCATION:Bangalore International Centre\, 7\, 4th Main Road\, Domlur II Stage\, Bangalore\, Karnataka\, 560071\, India
CATEGORIES:Books,Business,Gender
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bangaloreinternationalcentre.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Thumbnail-BBBR.jpg
